  ('144196981662398241', 'Bright Night', 2015, 'Drama, Mystery', 'Florian Gottschick', null, 'Anna Grisebach, Vladimir Burlakov, Benno Fürmann, Kai Ivo Baulitz, Gudrun Ritter, Michael Gwisdek, Ines Buchmann', null, 'A drama with a supernatural edge, this genre-crossing gem finds two couples visiting a home from their past, and sexual tension that brings out the worst in each other. Long-buried grudges resurface and it seems unlikely the couples will return intact. Faced with an outcome that will upset their delicate balance of happiness, the world offers them a bizarre opportunity to correct it.', 'A drama with a supernatural edge, this genre-crossing gem finds two couples visiting a home from their past, and sexual tension that brings out the worst in each other. Long-buried grudges resurface and it seems unlikely the couples will return intact. Faced with an outcome that will upset their delicate balance of happiness, the world offers them a bizarre opportunity to correct it.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/mdnW96hWUEeV2y2bbC0T1LGtvDW.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:315112'),
  ('370323050667081715', 'Bright Nights', 2017, 'Drama', 'Thomas Arslan, Reinhold Vorschneider', 'Thomas Arslan', 'Georg Friedrich, Tristan Göbel, Marie Leuenberger, Hanna Karlberg, Aggie Peterson, Frank Arne Olsen, Helle Goldman, Sigurd Kornelius Lakseide', null, 'A father tries to rekindle his relationship with his son after years of absence and lack of communication. He takes him on a car ride across northern Norway, hoping it is not too late.', 'A father tries to rekindle his relationship with his son after years of absence and lack of communication. He takes him on a car ride across northern Norway, hoping it is not too late.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/1cUP5kJ7GuerBbU0irKQwijtuYa.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:436345'),
  ('960069126044080648', 'Bright Spin', 2012, 'Comedy, Drama', 'Lucien Jean-Baptiste, Philippe Larue, Renaud Chassaing', 'Philippe Larue, Lucien Jean-Baptiste', 'Lucien Jean-Baptiste, Édouard Montoute, Magaly Berdy, Marie-Sohna Condé, Loreyna Colombo, Josias Lechertier, Marilou Perian Gizolme, José Dalmat', null, 'Patrick moved to France to become a renowned historian. After learning his mother is about to die, he returns to Martinique and embraces his roots.', 'Patrick moved to France to become a renowned historian. After learning his mother is about to die, he returns to Martinique and embraces his roots.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/kUmBtxUYBMbWt1kC4EkANgcyY78.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:127489'),
  ('916440125087708872', 'Bright Star', 2009, 'Drama, Romance', 'Jane Campion, David Hindle, Greig Fraser', 'Jane Campion', 'Abbie Cornish, Ben Whishaw, Paul Schneider, Kerry Fox, Edie Martin, Thomas Brodie-Sangster, Claudie Blakley, Gerard Monaco', 'PG', 'In 1818, high-spirited young Fanny Brawne finds herself increasingly intrigued by the handsome but aloof poet John Keats, who lives next door to her family friends the Dilkes. After reading a book of his poetry, she finds herself even more drawn to the taciturn Keats. Although he agrees to teach her about poetry, Keats cannot act on his reciprocated feelings for Fanny, since as a struggling poet he has no money to support a wife.', 'In 1818, high-spirited young Fanny Brawne finds herself increasingly intrigued by the handsome but aloof poet John Keats, who lives next door to her family friends the Dilkes. After reading a book of his poetry, she finds herself even more drawn to the taciturn Keats. Although he agrees to teach her about poetry, Keats cannot act on his reciprocated feelings for Fanny, since as a struggling poet he has no money to support a wife.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/csN6y4nq2kaBiegHaGw0DGp4plf.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:29963'),
  ('445640377770511552', 'Bright Victory', 1951, 'Drama, Romance', 'William H. Daniels, Mark Robson, John Sherwood', 'Robert Buckner', 'Arthur Kennedy, Peggy Dow, Julie Adams, James Edwards, Will Geer, Nana Bryant, Jim Backus, Minor Watson', 'NR', 'A soldier blinded in war returns home and attempts to adjust to civilian life.', 'A soldier blinded in war returns home and attempts to adjust to civilian life.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/hLWLDciSgrmYlNIxGjehl5qOTTy.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:109258'),
  ('74363573052957696', 'Bright Young Things', 2003, 'Comedy', 'Stephen Fry, Cordelia Hardy, Matthew Penry-Davey', 'Stephen Fry', 'Stephen Campbell Moore, Emily Mortimer, Harriet Walter, Michael Sheen, James McAvoy, David Tennant, Stockard Channing, Fenella Woolgar', 'R', 'During the 1930s in England, a group of young socialites dominate the national gossip with extravagant and outlandish antics. Among the group is the aspiring novelist Adam Fenwick-Symes, who is attempting to raise enough money to marry fellow member Nina Blount. However, after customs officials confiscate his first manuscript, Fenwick-Symes must recover from the financial setback and figure out new ways to earn money for a wedding.', 'During the 1930s in England, a group of young socialites dominate the national gossip with extravagant and outlandish antics. Among the group is the aspiring novelist Adam Fenwick-Symes, who is attempting to raise enough money to marry fellow member Nina Blount. However, after customs officials confiscate his first manuscript, Fenwick-Symes must recover from the financial setback and figure out new ways to earn money for a wedding.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/m7ik01FJKBSEoy0L0PKz7eEf9kI.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:15271'),
  ('329946868116436321', 'Bright: Samurai Soul', 2021, 'Animation, Action, Fantasy', 'Kyohei Ishiguro', 'Michiko Yokote', 'Yuuki Nomura, Daisuke Hirakawa, Shion Wakayama, MIYAVI, Maaya Sakamoto, Kenjiro Tsuda, Chafurin, Mamoru Miyano', 'PG-13', 'Izo, a Ronin, and Raiden, an orc, work to bring a young elf girl and the wand she carries to the land of the elves in the north.', 'Izo, a Ronin, and Raiden, an orc, work to bring a young elf girl and the wand she carries to the land of the elves in the north.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/6FuOW69wl9Bf2kzaVut596sMhZ6.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:839100'),
  ('865933837114839923', 'Brightburn', 2019, 'Horror, Science Fiction', 'Gene Michael Smith, Jacques Terblanche, Allie Toman', 'Brian Gunn, Mark Gunn', 'Jackson A. Dunn, Elizabeth Banks, David Denman, Matt Jones, Meredith Hagner, Becky Wahlstrom, Emmie Hunter, Gregory Alan Williams', 'R', 'What if a child from another world crash-landed on Earth, but instead of becoming a hero to mankind, he proved to be something far more sinister?', 'What if a child from another world crash-landed on Earth, but instead of becoming a hero to mankind, he proved to be something far more sinister?', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/sJWwkYc9ajwnPRSkqj8Aue5JbKz.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:531309'),
  ('636913324432410098', 'Brighton Beach Memoirs', 1986, 'Comedy', 'Gene Saks, John Bailey', 'Neil Simon', 'Jonathan Silverman, Blythe Danner, Stacey Glick, Lisa Waltz, Judith Ivey, Bob Dishy, Brian Drillinger, James Handy', 'PG-13', 'Eugene, a young teenage Jewish boy, recalls his memoirs of his time as an adolescent youth. He lives with his parents, his aunt, two cousins, and his brother, Stanley, whom he looks up to and admires. He goes through the hardships of puberty, sexual fantasy, and living the life of a poor boy in a crowded house.', 'Eugene, a young teenage Jewish boy, recalls his memoirs of his time as an adolescent youth. He lives with his parents, his aunt, two cousins, and his brother, Stanley, whom he looks up to and admires. He goes through the hardships of puberty, sexual fantasy, and living the life of a poor boy in a crowded house.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/gtaQOHgnGAOQdkLY57Mlu0ZdZA3.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:32060'),
  ('885172274412748120', 'Brighton Rock', 1948, 'Crime, Drama, Thriller', 'Harry Waxman, John Boulting, Gerry Mitchell', 'Graham Greene, Terence Rattigan', 'Richard Attenborough, Hermione Baddeley, William Hartnell, Nigel Stock, Wylie Watson, Carol Marsh, Harcourt Williams, Virginia Winter', null, 'Centring on the activities of a gang of assorted criminals and, in particular, their leader – a vicious young hoodlum known as "Pinkie" – the film''s main thematic concern is the criminal underbelly evident in inter-war Brighton.', 'Centring on the activities of a gang of assorted criminals and, in particular, their leader – a vicious young hoodlum known as "Pinkie" – the film''s main thematic concern is the criminal underbelly evident in inter-war Brighton.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/pNzK7KEY30dgI9rfbTvolzNVZie.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:13385'),
