  ('631129672154844273', 'Café Lumière', 2004, 'Drama', 'Hou Hsiao-hsien, Mark Lee Ping-Bing, Fumio Nomoto', 'Hou Hsiao-hsien, Chu Tien-Wen', 'Yo Hitoto, Tadanobu Asano, Masato Hagiwara, Kimiko Yo, Nenji Kobayashi, Yôko Hoshi, Keiichi Asada, Yukio Endô', 'NR', 'In a distinctly contemporary Tokyo that looks backwards to the city’s disappearing past, Yoko is a writer investigating the life of a modernist composer of the 1930s. She is pregnant by a man she does not want to marry and has found a kindred spirit in a used bookstore owner who aids her research.', 'In a distinctly contemporary Tokyo that looks backwards to the city’s disappearing past, Yoko is a writer investigating the life of a modernist composer of the 1930s. She is pregnant by a man she does not want to marry and has found a kindred spirit in a used bookstore owner who aids her research.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/mvXQlk3mZnfJkzZg13Mt7qPstMF.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:52512'),
